  "invariants": [
    {
      "id": "INVARIANT-0a668fd2",
      "text": "Every label span is stored as code-point character offsets {start,end} into the raw text; raw secret/PII text never appears in annotations, exports, or the review DOM (offset-only, W3C TextPositionSelector).",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:25.328Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "INVARIANT-be46e959",
      "text": "Secret and PII scanning run fully offline in the sensitive path: no live verification or network calls (detect-secrets -n / no --verification).",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q5",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:25.403Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "INVARIANT-efac03a9",
      "text": "Per-record audit metadata (reviewer, timestamp, model version, policy version) is stored as columns on each record; the audit log is append-only, stores HMAC hashes not plaintext, and fails closed.",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q8",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:25.473Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "INVARIANT-36e24b71",
      "text": "Thread/document grouping has no cross-split leakage: an entire source thread is assigned wholly to a single dataset split.",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q7",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:25.550Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "INVARIANT-e708cc98",
      "text": "Authorization is enforced server-side; unredacted spans are returned only on an explicit, logged, policy-permitted request.",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q8",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:25.612Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "DECISION-ea8f447b",
      "title": "v1 scope = thin end-to-end slice",
      "text": "First implementation builds every DAG stage in its simplest honest form, single-reviewer, no orchestrator. Defer adjudication queue (flat needs-second-look flag), IAA, multi-reviewer, multi-tenant RBAC.",
      "status": "accepted",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q1",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:01.772Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DECISION-9acea95a",
      "title": "No orchestrator in v1; DB-state HITL, Prefect later",
      "text": "Human-review pause is DB state (pending_review table flipped by the review API); a plain worker loop advances records. Keep review state in our own DB so orchestrator choice stays reversible; adopt Prefect when multi-batch retries/observability are needed. Temporal only if waits reach weeks.",
      "status": "accepted",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q2",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:01.861Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DECISION-ef8c46ce",
      "title": "Thin custom React review tool, not off-the-shelf",
      "text": "Build a one-screen annotation/review tool (accept/rewrite/skip/reject/escalate) storing only {doc_id,start,end,label}. Rejected Label Studio CE (review/IAA Enterprise-only), Prodigy (commercial), Argilla (maintenance-only)/Doccano (no adjudication).",
      "status": "accepted",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q3",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:01.933Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DECISION-c999315f",
      "title": "spaCy owns offsets; no destructive normalize in v1",
      "text": "Keep raw text verbatim (doc.text==input_text); use Doc.char_span(strict) whose None return is the invalid-span signal. No normalized->raw index map. If normalization is later needed, prefer HF library-tracked normalizers over a hand-rolled map.",
      "status": "accepted",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q4",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:01.997Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DECISION-5c3235cc",
      "title": "PII/secret scan = Presidio + offline secret scanner",
      "text": "Presidio for entity PII + custom PatternRecognizers for Bearer/sk- tokens; detect-secrets --no-verify (or gitleaks stdin) for key long-tail; merge spans, secret-scanner wins on overlap. Redaction via Presidio Anonymizer, all in-environment.",
      "status": "accepted",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q5",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:02.063Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DECISION-3ac08160",
      "title": "Pydantic per-record validation; Pandera dataset-gate later",
      "text": "One Pydantic model is both the SLM output contract and the validation gate; cross-field span rules and conditional-required evidence live in @model_validator(mode=after). Add Pandera at dataset level once batches are large.",
      "status": "accepted",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q6",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:02.122Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DECISION-9192c6f9",
      "title": "DVC + thread-grouped JSONL; HF datasets for trainer",
      "text": "Version data/<thread_id>.jsonl with DVC + private remote; per-record audit as JSONL columns. Emit HF datasets splits for the SLM trainer; thread-grouping enforced by our own split logic. Move to lakeFS if hook-enforced audit fields are wanted.",
      "status": "accepted",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q7",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:02.186Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DECISION-cdd091a6",
      "title": "Minimal-but-correct-shaped access/audit in v1",
      "text": "Single reviewer role; API returns redacted text by default, serves unredacted span only on explicit logged view_unredacted; append-only HMAC audit that fails closed. Add RBAC/ABAC + policy engine when a second reviewer or sensitivity tier exists.",
      "status": "accepted",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q8",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:02.265Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DECISION-8b485576",
      "title": "Python backend + thin React/TS review UI",
      "text": "Backend in Python (Presidio, spaCy, Pydantic, DVC, HF datasets native). One small React/TS screen for review; server-rendered + vanilla JS acceptable to start. Rejected Streamlit (awkward span interaction, harder to make privacy-safe).",
      "status": "accepted",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/03-design-discussion-pipeline-architecture.md#Q9",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:02.345Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DECISION-46422d7c",
      "title": "03-design stack supersedes task.md",
      "text": "Approving SPEC.md confirms the 03-design-discussion tech stack (Python: Presidio, spaCy, Pydantic, DVC, HF datasets; thin review screen) supersedes task.md's 'stack not yet decided'. Resolves ASSUMPTION-fd80e5a6 stack question.",
      "status": "accepted",
      "source": "SPEC.md approval by Aamir Alam",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T19:27:01.831Z",
      "paths": [],
      "tags": []
    }
  ],
  "knowledge": [
    {
      "id": "KNOWLEDGE-d308c87f",
      "title": "Offsets are the universal span contract",
      "text": "Every surveyed tool (Presidio, spaCy, HF fast tokenizers, W3C selector, Label Studio/Argilla/Doccano/Prodigy) represents spans as {start,end} char offsets, so offset preservation is the integration seam tying intake->annotation->validation together.",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/02-research-labeling-pipeline-ecosystem.md",
      "tags": [],
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:25.677Z",
      "paths": []
    },
    {
      "id": "KNOWLEDGE-869f3cc6",
      "title": "Presidio lacks built-in secret entities",
      "text": "Presidio has no built-in API_KEY/BEARER_TOKEN entity; keys/tokens come from secret scanners (gitleaks/trufflehog/detect-secrets, all accept stdin) or custom PatternRecognizers. Scanner verification makes live network calls - disable for sensitive data.",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/02-research-labeling-pipeline-ecosystem.md",
      "tags": [],
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:25.740Z",
      "paths": []
    },
    {
      "id": "KNOWLEDGE-3d6925a6",
      "title": "spaCy gives a free invalid-span signal",
      "text": "spaCy guarantees doc.text==input_text; Doc.char_span(start,end,alignment_mode=strict) returns None when offsets do not land on token boundaries, which is a natural invalid-span signal. Length checks are NOT proof offsets survived normalization.",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/02-research-labeling-pipeline-ecosystem.md",
      "tags": [],
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:25.804Z",
      "paths": []
    },
    {
      "id": "KNOWLEDGE-e61fe935",
      "title": "HITL pause separates the orchestrators",
      "text": "Native human-wait pause/resume: Temporal (durable signals, years), Airflow 3.1+ (HITL operators), Prefect (pause/suspend with Pydantic form). Dagster has no pause primitive (issue 14681) and needs a split-run+sensor workaround.",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/02-research-labeling-pipeline-ecosystem.md",
      "tags": [],
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:25.880Z",
      "paths": []
    },
    {
      "id": "KNOWLEDGE-fe5759c9",
      "title": "Per-record audit belongs in columns",
      "text": "Across DVC/lakeFS/HF datasets/Delta/Git-LFS, per-record audit (reviewer/timestamp/model/policy) lives as record columns; commit/tag metadata only carries batch-level facts. Grouping by thread is always a self-defined partition, never an automatic no-leakage guarantee.",
      "source": ".humanlayer/tasks/design-data-labeling-pipeline-architecture-micksk/02-research-labeling-pipeline-ecosystem.md",
      "tags": [],
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-07T14:37:25.950Z",
      "paths": []
    },
    {
